  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $434$\n\nII. $785$\n\nIII. $587$",
  "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $434,$ we have that \n\n$$\n43-2(4)=43-8=35\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $434$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $785,$ we have that \n\n$$\n78-2(5)=78-10=68\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $785$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $587,$ we have that \n\n$$\n58-2(7)=58-14=44\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $587$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
